Wearing the XTRATUF Legacy while boating in Alaska.

To ensure that we reviewed the best boots for the rainy season, we researched the most popular rain boots and came up with over 30 different choices.

We tested rain boots on soggy Alaska trails, in rivers in Maine, on commutes in the Pacific Northwest, and during farmwork in Iowa. We tested on long walks in New York City, while digging out a flooded house in California, cleaning out the chicken coop in Portland, Oregon, and guiding clients on rafting trips. We also tested waterproof hiking boots in Iceland, Colorado, Washington, and Tennessee. In all, we’ve spent over four years testing rain boots and waterproof boots for women.

To be considered for each winning category, we measured each pair of boots against standardized criteria: good tread, waterproofness, great fit, and ease of pulling on and taking off. For our waterproof recommendations, the boots had to be considered waterproof (or at least water resistant) by our own testing and a majority of customer reviews. We also included a water-resistant option for everyday walking.

